{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC VERIFICATION — ALL 16 CRITERIA VERIFIED against merged code and recorded comments, then ticked.\nVerified by a held-out subagent briefed with the operator scope ruling, then spot-checked by me.\nFive commits confirmed ancestors of origin/main (07d19c5537e1, efdae15505b4, 5e54e1c081ca, plus the\n62ac and 635f parity fixes).\n\nTHE TWO REAL BARS — payload parity and tool parity — both PROVEN BY CAPTURE, not by reading code:\n  PAYLOAD: system prompt 60 chars BYTE-IDENTICAL; 1 user message 2486 chars BYTE-IDENTICAL;\n    max_tokens 16000/16000; temperature matching; the model id is the ONLY differing field. Both slots,\n    with and without a requested temperature. Method: Anthropic arm captured via httpx.MockTransport on a\n    real SDK-assembled body; Bedrock arm via a real boto3 bedrock-runtime client with only converse\n    intercepted. Zero network, zero tokens.\n    Gated by test_the_outbound_payload_is_equivalent_across_providers[standard|frontier]\n    (tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py:539) which asserts differing == [] for every normalized field\n    except model_id AND asserts the capture is non-empty, so it cannot pass on an empty capture.\n    The 8 legitimate envelope differences are enumerated in ENVELOPE_DIFFERENCES (:398-415) and pinned by\n    test_the_enumerated_envelope_differences_are_the_only_ones_normalized (:587) — so a NEW difference\n    appearing would fail rather than be silently normalized away.\n  TOOLS: 6 tools identical on both providers (comment_ticket, list_directory, read_file, resolve_symbol,\n    search_files, show_ticket) — names, descriptions and input schemas compared as sorted JSON.\n    Gated at :556; asserts the tool list is non-empty first, so it cannot prove parity vacuously.\n  CAPABILITY DIFFERENCE: exactly ONE, and it is MODEL-driven, not provider-driven — with temperature=0.0\n    requested, sonnet sends it on BOTH providers and opus withdraws it on BOTH, via\n    _MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES supports_temperature: False. Pinned at :567. Mutation evidence\n    recorded: deleting the opus override turns that test RED.\n  PROVIDER-CLEAN ROUTING: standard v2 {bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6: 84}, frontier v2\n    {bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8: 84}, NON-BEDROCK CALLS {} on both. Split-brain risk pinned by\n    test_each_arms_config_reaches_every_worker_under_concurrency (:192) under concurrency=6.\n\nSPOT-CHECKED BY ME, not taken on trust: the four named tests exist at the cited lines; the\nno-CI-invocation grep returns exit 1 (harness never runs in a workflow, also regression-pinned at :368);\nboth artifact slots are measured with n_gold=28 and epochs=3; and the offline module is green with\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY / AWS_* stripped — 23 passed.\n\nUNDER THE OPERATOR SCOPE RULING: the residual gating_failures in the artifact (standard 1 flip; frontier\nagreement 0.929 + 2 flips) are cross-model verdict comparisons and are INFORMATIONAL, not gates. Both\nslots therefore carry passed=False while no acceptance criterion is unmet — the criteria require the\nartifact to CARRY those blocks, which it does, not to report passed=True. Nothing is rescoped that\ncomment 16 had not already retargeted.\n\nBEDROCK CLEARS THE BAR AS THE EPIC DEFINES IT: same payloads reach the LLM, same tools are available,\nrouting is provider-clean, and both inference profiles invoke. That is the confirmation the eb6e cutover\nhold was waiting on.\n\nONE BLEMISH, RECORDED NOT HIDDEN: the artifact metrics.latency_s now reads 0.0/0.0 because the post-62ac\nre-score recomputes from records, which carry no latency. The REAL live figures are preserved — at slot\nlevel in the JSON (frontier v1 2103.3 / v2 2105.3; standard v1 2756.6 / v2 2484.8), in comment 13, and in\ngit at 72f863b5a2. No criterion requires the artifact to carry them. No data lost.\n\nTHE cachePoint TTL ITEM THIS TICKET DEFERRED TO S8 IS NOW ANSWERED, on 1aa2: Bedrock cachePoint takes an\nOPTIONAL ttl DEFAULTING TO 5 MINUTES — the same default Anthropic cache_control applies. The premise that\nBedrock \"carries no TTL\" was wrong; there is no substantive difference to carry forward."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785769683723050001,"uuid":"759835d7-b1b6-4b76-a1d0-92e65cfb8717"}